"""NEW8 candidate designs -- frozen data (2026-10-27;
seven more designs added 2026-10-28, four second-best
designs added 2026-10-28 phase 2).

Equations, conditions, exit multipliers and walk scores
of the NEW8 candidate designs installed in this build,
transcribed from the programme DISCOVERY JSONs
(~/workspace/fx/work_new8/MONTH_*_DISCOVERY.json). The
walk score of each equation is the value the research
walk itself used (the stored candidate ledgers'
per-strategy score; axis-key formula cross-checked in
work_29load/replay_research.py and, for the 2026-10-28
designs, work_29load/gen_designs2.py, zero mismatches).
Feature groups name the new8_features blocks the
design's conditions need on top of the base block.

2026-10-28 designs: jun_b9 / sep_b9 / sep_b9c (Plan B-9),
sep_b9sb (Plan B-9 Track B R14, September second best
under the user's scoped waiver), apr_q09 (Plan B-2 Q09
with its 11 dollar-index equations EXCLUDED -- the
28-symbol app ships zero dollar-trading equations),
apr_pvote (P-VOTE) and nov_pbranchc (P-BRANCH Plan C
OR-branch design; each equation carries 'branches',
each branch with its own conditions, exit pair and
hold; the equation score is the best branch axis key).

2026-10-28 phase-2 designs (second bests installed on
the user's order, waiving each scan's NEARLY items;
scores recomputed by standalone discovery evaluation
in work_29load/gen_designs3.py, cross-checked against
the stored ledgers, zero mismatches): dec_b6sb2 (Plan
B-6 SB-REDO R18, December), mar_b6sb2 (Plan B-6 SB-REDO
R17, March), nov_pbsb (P-BRANCH Track B R12 OR-branch,
November) and apr_pvsb (P-VOTE Track B fallback R13
vote-threshold, April). The b6 feature group (Plan B-6
nested nx_* combinations) was ported for the two B-6
designs and audited bit-exact against the research
frames.

2026-10-29 designs (lane-reconciliation winners;
scores recomputed by standalone discovery evaluation
in work_29load/gen_designs4.py, cross-checked against
the stored ledgers, zero mismatches): mar_rp (P-REPLACE
Track A C06, March -- slot-replacement design, see
core.cycle86c_best), nov_rp (P-REPLACE Track A C04,
November), dec_rg (P-REGIME Track A C07, December) and
dec_rgc (P-REGIME Plan C C07, December). The pr and rp
feature groups (regime / replacement transforms of the
planb9c superset columns) were ported for these designs
(core.new8_features.add_pr_columns / add_rp_columns)
and audited bit-exact against the research lane frames
(work_29load/check_pr_rp.py); the b3 block gained the
planb3 er10 column those transforms read.
"""
